{"project":"platform/upstream/llvm","branch":"aarch64_ilp32","topic":"aarch64ilp32","id":"Ic315745942fe43cbaeb314964e87034ec9343866","number":323901,"subject":"aarch64: use ULL for AUXV for ILP32","owner":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"url":"https://review.tizen.org/gerrit/c/platform/upstream/llvm/+/323901","hashtags":[],"createdOn":1746755252,"lastUpdated":1750653870,"open":true,"status":"NEW","comments":[{"timestamp":1746755252,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 1."},{"timestamp":1747029675,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Patch Set 1: Code-Review+1"},{"timestamp":1747065058,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"Patch Set 1: Code-Review-1\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1747065339,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"Patch Set 1:\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1749120684,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"Uploaded patch set 2.\n\nOutdated Votes:\n* Code-Review+1, Code-Review-1 (copy condition: \"changekind:NO_CHANGE OR is:MIN\")\n"},{"timestamp":1749127845,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"Patch Set 2:\n\n(5 comments)"},{"timestamp":1749138475,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1749207397,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"Patch Set 2: Code-Review-1\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1749207886,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"Patch Set 2: -Code-Review\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1749207987,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"Patch Set 2:\n\n(1 comment)"},{"timestamp":1749240611,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"Patch Set 2: Code-Review-2"},{"timestamp":1750653870,"reviewer":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"message":"Topic set to aarch64ilp32"}],"currentPatchSet":{"number":2,"revision":"3e7d27f7dbaade53888634622c3c19749bdffb58","parents":["e6a08018aba7f55d778d7aa20466cf52358fb0a2"],"ref":"refs/changes/01/323901/2","uploader":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"createdOn":1749120684,"author":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"-2","grantedOn":1749240611,"by":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"}}],"comments":[{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"@k.frolov@samsung.com\nNote, that HWCAP2_SME is also defined in many parts of code, not just one header.\nThis problem related to one that llvm, binutils and gcc is set of separate tools.\nThe only common part is include, but I don\u0027t want auxval_t to be in system with include.\n\nIt was possible to select it as common part only in glibc."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/aarch64/sme-abi-init.c","line":24,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving this definition to some header file and include it in all other .c files where you have similar definitions (at least in other three .c files)."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64.c","line":24,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving it to header file."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/hwcap.inc","line":176,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"when we use auxval_t in macros we cannot compare macros inside #if. Maybe not a big dealbut may be it is better to define auxval_t as a macro."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/lse_atomics/android.inc","line":12,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"back to design consideration: why do we change ulong to auxval_t if HWCAP_ATOMICS is small (1\u003c\u003c8)? It turns out to be so many changes in many packages"},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/lse_atomics/android.inc","line":12,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"Okay, as we discussed several days ago - let\u0027s apply some solution, to solve the issue, without trying push upstream for now."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_getauxval.h","line":38,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving this definition to separate .h file."},{"file":"libc/test/UnitTest/HermeticTestUtils.cpp","line":16,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"Again, I suggest moving this definition to separate .h file."},{"file":"openmp/runtime/src/kmp_runtime.cpp","line":7066,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I suggest moving this to separate .h file."}],"sizeInsertions":85,"sizeDeletions":40},"patchSets":[{"number":1,"revision":"0f32071a10b638a129df26f30e406279c6f6ce51","parents":["e6a08018aba7f55d778d7aa20466cf52358fb0a2"],"ref":"refs/changes/01/323901/1","uploader":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"},"createdOn":1746755252,"author":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"1","grantedOn":1747029675,"by":{"name":"Dongkyun Son","email":"dongkyun.s@samsung.com","username":"dkson95"}},{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"-1","grantedOn":1747065058,"by":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"}}],"comments":[{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"We discussed the changes from @i.maidanski@samsung.com, I will bring discussion of these changes to upstream to understand how correct they are"},{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"... how correct changes are"}],"sizeInsertions":78,"sizeDeletions":35},{"number":2,"revision":"3e7d27f7dbaade53888634622c3c19749bdffb58","parents":["e6a08018aba7f55d778d7aa20466cf52358fb0a2"],"ref":"refs/changes/01/323901/2","uploader":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"createdOn":1749120684,"author":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"kind":"REWORK","approvals":[{"type":"Code-Review","description":"Code-Review","value":"-2","grantedOn":1749240611,"by":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"}}],"comments":[{"file":"/PATCHSET_LEVEL","line":0,"reviewer":{"name":"Kudrevatykh Pavel","email":"absque.deo@gmail.com","username":"Pusha"},"message":"@k.frolov@samsung.com\nNote, that HWCAP2_SME is also defined in many parts of code, not just one header.\nThis problem related to one that llvm, binutils and gcc is set of separate tools.\nThe only common part is include, but I don\u0027t want auxval_t to be in system with include.\n\nIt was possible to select it as common part only in glibc."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/aarch64/sme-abi-init.c","line":24,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving this definition to some header file and include it in all other .c files where you have similar definitions (at least in other three .c files)."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64.c","line":24,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving it to header file."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/hwcap.inc","line":176,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"when we use auxval_t in macros we cannot compare macros inside #if. Maybe not a big dealbut may be it is better to define auxval_t as a macro."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/lse_atomics/android.inc","line":12,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"back to design consideration: why do we change ulong to auxval_t if HWCAP_ATOMICS is small (1\u003c\u003c8)? It turns out to be so many changes in many packages"},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/builtins/cpu_model/aarch64/lse_atomics/android.inc","line":12,"reviewer":{"name":"Ivan Maidanski","email":"i.maidanski@samsung.com","username":"imaidanski"},"message":"Okay, as we discussed several days ago - let\u0027s apply some solution, to solve the issue, without trying push upstream for now."},{"file":"compiler-rt/lib/sanitizer_common/sanitizer_getauxval.h","line":38,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"I propose moving this definition to separate .h file."},{"file":"libc/test/UnitTest/HermeticTestUtils.cpp","line":16,"reviewer":{"name":"Kirill Frolov","email":"k.frolov@samsung.com","username":"fk0"},"message":"Again, I suggest moving this definition to separate .h fil